es40 (AlphaServer ES40 emulator)

ES40 is an emulator for the DEC AlphaServer ES40 series originally
designed by Camiel Vanderhoeven. It can run operating systems that
support OpenVMS or Tru64 PALcode (e.g. OpenVMS, Windows 2000,
Tru64 UNIX, Linux, NetBSD, and OpenBSD).

The emulator supports SCSI, IDE, serial ports, sound, Ethernet (via
TUN/TAP and libpcap on Linux), and VGA graphics (via SDL3).

BUILD DEPENDENCIES:
This SlackBuild requires:
  - cmake-opt (CMake >= 3.24 is required upstream)
  - SDL3

NETWORKING:
To comply with offline build standards and avoid downloading external
crates from crates.io during compilation, the experimental Rust-based
userspace SLIRP NAT backend is disabled (-DES40_DISABLE_SLIRP=ON).
Full networking remains available on Linux using native TUN/TAP or
bridged Ethernet via libpcap.

FIRMWARE & ROMS:
To run ES40, you will need Alpha firmware (SRM console PALcode ROM,
such as cl67srmrom.exe / es40.rom). If using VGA graphics, you will
also need an S3 Trio64 VBIOS ROM image (e.g., 86c764x1.bin).

CONFIGURATION:
Use the configuration utility (es40-cfg, es40_cfg_tui, or es40_cfg_sdl)
to generate an initial configuration before running es40, ensuring all
required chipset devices are included. A fully documented reference
configuration is installed at /usr/doc/es40-<version>/es40.cfg.

SERIAL CONSOLE:
By default, the serial console opens a telnet listener on port 21264.
You can connect to it using standard telnet or PuTTY:
  telnet localhost 21264
